### Once upon a time
  -> Once upon a time, there was a big mountain. On top of the mountain, there was a small house. In the house, a boy named Tom lived with his mom and dad. They were very happy. / One day, Tom felt sad. He wanted to play with his friends, but they were all busy. He looked out the window and saw the mountain. It was so big and impressive. Tom wanted to go outside and play. / Tom's mom saw him sad. She said, "Tom, I will allow you to go outside and play with your friends." Tom was very happy. He put on his shoes and went outside. He played with his friends all day. They had so much fun. And that is how Tom and his friends had the best day ever.
  -> Once upon a time, in a small town, there was a little girl named Lucy. Lucy loved to play with her soft, fluffy cat, Whiskers. One day, Lucy and Whiskers went to the park to play with their friends. / At the park, Lucy saw her friend Timmy. Timmy was sitting on a bench, and he looked sad. Lucy asked, "Timmy, why are you sad?" Timmy said, "I lost my toy. Can you help me find it?" / Lucy wanted to help Timmy. They looked all around the park. Lucy kneeled down and started to look under the bench. She found the toy! Timmy was very happy, and they all played together in the park. / In the end, Lucy, Timmy, and their friends had a fun day at the park. They learned that helping others can make you happy too. And Whiskers, the soft, fluffy cat, was always there to help Lucy.
  -> Once upon a time, there was a little girl named Lily. She had a special toy, a big, red ball. Lily played with her ball every day. She was very proud of her ball because it could bounce high. / One sunny day, Lily and her friends went to the park to play. They saw a pretty light up in the sky. The light was very bright and shiny. Lily knew something would happen to her ball. She put the ball on the ground and let it bounce high up into the sky. / As the ball bounced, it turned into a big, bright ball. Lily and her friends were so happy. They played with the ball all day long. They knew that their hard work had paid off. And from that day on, Lily became known as the best ball player in the park.

