### One day, a little bird could not fly. It
  -> One day, a little bird could not fly. It was sad because it was hungry. The bird sat on a branch and started to cry. A kind squirrel saw the bird and wanted to help. / "Hello, bird," said the squirrel. "Why are you sad?" The bird told the squirrel that it was hungry and could not fly. The squirrel thought for a moment and said, "I know what to do. I will give you some of my nuts. They will be enough for you." / The bird was happy and ate the nuts. But then, something unexpected happened. The bird started to grow bigger and bigger! The squirrel was surprised and said, "Wow, bird! You are growing so fast!" / Now, the bird and the squirrel were friends. They played together every day and had many fun adventures. The bird never felt hungry again, because it had a new friend in the kind squirrel.
  -> One day, a little bird could not fly. It was sad. The bird had a friend, a kind old owl. The owl saw the bird was sad and wanted to help. The owl knew how to make the bird feel better. / The owl had an idea. It told the bird to eat good food and rest. The bird thought this was a good idea. Soon, the bird started to feel better. It could fly again. The bird was very happy. It thanked the owl and flew high in the sky. / The bird learned that when we feel sad, it is good to ask for help. The moral of the story is that friends should help each other feel better.
  -> One day, a little bird could not fly. It was sad. The bird had a friend, a big bear. The bear wanted to help the bird fly. They tried and tried, but the bird still could not fly. The bear felt bad for the bird. / Then, something unexpected happened. The bird saw a fake bird, not a bird. The bird wanted to fly, but it could not. The bear had an idea. They would ask the other animals for help. The animals thought it was a good idea. / The bird, the bear, and the other animals worked together. The bear used its strong arms to lift the bird up. The bird tried to fly. The bird flapped its wings and, to their surprise, it started to fly! The bird was so happy. The animals were happy too. The moral of the story is that when we work together, we can do anything.

